# ── AI providers ──
#
# WHERE each provider lives is in providers.json (endpoints, model names, vision).
# WHAT unlocks it is here. Keys never go in providers.json — that file is committed,
# this one is not.
#
# A provider whose key is missing simply doesn't appear in the model dropdown.
# Uncomment the ones you have. You need at least one.
#
# Check what's actually available:  python providers.py

# ── Where your data lives ─────────────────────────────────────────────────
# output/, references/, ditherra.db AND secrets.json all sit under this root.
# Defaults to the repo itself, which is what a local run wants. Point it
# somewhere else for a mounted volume, or a second install that must not share
# sprites and keys with the first.
# DITHERRA_DATA=/path/to/your/data

# Ollama — free, local, no key needed at all. Just have it running:
#   ollama pull qwen3:8b
# The app asks Ollama what you have pulled, so there's nothing to list here.

# GEMINI_API_KEY=            # aistudio.google.com/apikey — chat + concept art
# OPENAI_API_KEY=            # platform.openai.com
# OPENAI_BASE_URL=           # point openai at a compatible server (vLLM, LiteLLM, proxy)
# DEEPSEEK_API_KEY=          # platform.deepseek.com — cheap, good at tool calling
# DASHSCOPE_API_KEY=         # Alibaba Qwen (incl. qwen-vl for vision)
# ZHIPU_API_KEY=             # Zhipu GLM
# MOONSHOT_API_KEY=          # Moonshot Kimi
# GROQ_API_KEY=              # very fast, generous free tier
# OPENROUTER_API_KEY=        # one key, hundreds of models — the :free ones cost nothing

# Codex uses its own ChatGPT login from Settings, never OPENAI_API_KEY or ~/.codex.
# DITHERRA_CODEX_HOME=       # optional isolated profile location
# CODEX_BINARY=              # optional full path when `codex` is not on PATH

# Antigravity / gemini-cli: signing in there leaves OAuth credentials in
# ~/.gemini/oauth_creds.json, and those cover BOTH chat and concept art — no
# separate Gemini key needed.
# ANTIGRAVITY_PROJECT_ID=    # defaults to default-cli-project

# Google Cloud service account instead of a Gemini API key:
# GOOGLE_SERVICE_ACCOUNT_JSON=service-account.json
# GOOGLE_SERVICE_ACCOUNT_JSON_CONTENT={"type":"service_account",...}

# ── Optional: tracing ──
# LangChain reads these on its own — nothing in this repo imports LangSmith.

# LANGSMITH_TRACING=true
# LANGSMITH_API_KEY=
# LANGSMITH_PROJECT=ditherra

# ── Optional: server ──

# HOST=0.0.0.0             # reach it from another device — set API_KEY too if you do
# PORT=8500
# DEV=1                    # backend auto-reload while editing code
# API_KEY=                 # require an x-api-key header on every request
# CORS_ORIGINS=http://localhost:3000

# ── Free-tier concept art ──────────────────────────────────────────────
# Pollinations: FLUX and friends on a free tier. Speaks OpenAI's own image
# endpoint, so nothing else is needed. Key: https://enter.pollinations.ai/keys
# POLLINATIONS_API_KEY=sk_...

# Cloudflare Workers AI: 10,000 neurons/day free, resets 00:00 UTC, runs
# FLUX.1 [schnell]. Needs BOTH — the account id is the one in your dashboard
# URL and is not a secret, the token is.
# CLOUDFLARE_API_TOKEN=...
# CLOUDFLARE_ACCOUNT_ID=...

# Seconds a single model call may take before it is abandoned. The default is
# generous because a small local model can legitimately take minutes; lower it
# if you only use fast cloud providers and want failures to surface sooner.
# DITHERRA_LLM_TIMEOUT=600

# Ollama defaults to a 4096-token context on machines with little VRAM, which
# this agent outgrows a few turns into a 32x32 sprite — and Ollama truncates
# silently, dropping the system prompt first. Raise it before you start Ollama:
#   launchctl setenv OLLAMA_CONTEXT_LENGTH 32768   (macOS)
#   OLLAMA_CONTEXT_LENGTH=32768 ollama serve       (Linux)
